    explanation: "Interviewers ask this to assess whether you can manage paid campaigns as a measurable acquisition system rather than focusing only on clicks.\n\nWhat the interviewer wants:\n- Explain targeting, bidding, creative, landing pages, and tracking as one funnel.\n- Use the correct performance metric to diagnose the problem.\n- Show how the decision affects acquisition cost and business value.",
    sampleAnswer: "In most PPC platforms, ad position and cost are determined by an auction combining the advertiser's bid with a relevance/quality signal (like Quality Score), not bid amount alone ? which is why a lower bid with strong relevance can beat a higher bid with poor relevance. Manual bidding lets the advertiser set bid amounts directly at the keyword or campaign level, giving full control but requiring active, ongoing management. Automated bidding strategies (target CPA, target ROAS, maximize conversions) use the platform's machine learning to adjust bids in real time based on signals like device, time of day, and user behavior, generally performing better with enough conversion data to learn from, but offering less granular manual control and requiring trust in the platform's optimization.",
    detailedAnswer: "**Direct answer:**\n\nIn most PPC platforms, ad position and cost are determined by an auction combining the advertiser's bid with a relevance/quality signal (like Quality Score), not bid amount alone ? which is why a lower bid with strong relevance can beat a higher bid with poor relevance. Manual bidding lets the advertiser set bid amounts directly at the keyword or campaign level, giving full control but requiring active, ongoing management. Automated bidding strategies (target CPA, target ROAS, maximize conversions) use the platform's machine learning to adjust bids in real time based on signals like device, time of day, and user behavior, generally performing better with enough conversion data to learn from, but offering less granular manual control and requiring trust in the platform's optimization.\n\n**Example:**\n\nA campaign with steady conversion volume and a clear target cost-per-acquisition is a good candidate for automated Target CPA bidding, letting the algorithm adjust bids per auction based on signals a human manager couldn't realistically evaluate in real time. A brand-new campaign with little historical conversion data might start with manual or maximize-clicks bidding until enough data accumulates for automated strategies to optimize effectively.",
