    sampleAnswer: "Move beyond channel metrics (clicks, impressions, even conversions logged in the ad platform itself) to business-level outcomes: incremental revenue, customer acquisition cost relative to customer lifetime value, and, ideally, a way to estimate what would have happened without the campaign ? through a holdout/control group, a geo-based incrementality test, or comparing a launch period against a comparable prior period adjusted for seasonality. Ad-platform-reported conversions alone can overstate true incremental impact, since some of those conversions would have happened anyway (a customer who was already going to buy, credited to a retargeting ad they happened to see).",
    detailedAnswer: "**Direct answer:**\n\nMove beyond channel metrics (clicks, impressions, even conversions logged in the ad platform itself) to business-level outcomes: incremental revenue, customer acquisition cost relative to customer lifetime value, and, ideally, a way to estimate what would have happened without the campaign ? through a holdout/control group, a geo-based incrementality test, or comparing a launch period against a comparable prior period adjusted for seasonality. Ad-platform-reported conversions alone can overstate true incremental impact, since some of those conversions would have happened anyway (a customer who was already going to buy, credited to a retargeting ad they happened to see).\n\n**Example:**\n\nA retargeting campaign reports $50,000 in attributed conversions, but a holdout test ? withholding the ads from a random subset of the eligible audience ? shows that group converted at nearly the same rate anyway, suggesting a large share of the platform-attributed revenue wasn't actually incremental and would have happened without the ad spend.",
